From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode-port <port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:04:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] D209 core: removing a session admits no notices from the work
 it cancels

Upstream: deleting a session whose background subagent is still running cancels the subagent's job, whose
completion notice ("Subagent cancelled") is then admitted into the session being deleted and wakes it. The wake
starts an execution after the session is gone: session.execution.started is published for the deleted session,
and settling it fails with a FOREIGN KEY constraint error ("Failed to publish Session execution lifecycle").
Fixed: while a session is being removed, synthetic admissions into it (how background work reports back) fail
with Session.NotFoundError, so the cancellation is not reported to it and nothing wakes it.
Scenarios: project-jobs.test.ts "deleting a session cancels its background jobs" (the notice and the execution
after session.deleted are gone)
Upstream tests: packages/core/test/session-remove.test.ts adds a test

